[gd_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" load_steps=2 format=3]

; The plasma shell a capital ship throws when it goes: a committed .png laid
; FLAT ON THE BATTLE PLANE, not facing the camera.
;
; That orientation is the point of it. A front expanding through a plane is a
; ring seen in perspective, and the ellipse it makes tells the eye which plane
; the ship was flying in. Billboarded, the same ring reads as a bubble, and a
; bubble belongs to nothing.
;
; BLUE, and that is the other point. Every other layer of an explosion is
; painted in the fire colours, which are the oranges the damage report and the
; collision chips wear. A shell in the blues reads as something else entirely:
; not the hull burning, but the reactor's containment letting go and washing
; out through it. A frigate's magazine cooking off does not do this, which is
; why the ring's strength is the nova dial and a small hull shows none of it.
;
; A StandardMaterial3D rather than fx_billboard.gdshader, which paints every
; other effect here. Not a fork: that shader's whole job is tinting untextured
; geometry from its own model space radius, and this is the one effect whose
; content is a picture. Sampling a texture from a spatial ShaderMaterial is
; also the one thing that does not work on the gl_compatibility renderer the
; Web target needs, while a StandardMaterial3D's own albedo map does, which is
; what the painted hulls have been proving since the first ship.
;
; Additive, because it is light passing through: the debris and the fire behind
; it stay visible as it washes over them, which is what sells it as a front
; rather than as a lid. Alpha scales what is added, so src.ui.explosion.gd
; fades the shell by writing albedo_color's alpha and the palette colours in
; the texture never shift.
;
; Nearest filtering, because the texture is pixel art like everything else in
; this game, and unshaded and two sided because a plasma front is not lit by
; the sun and is the same from underneath.

[ext_resource type="Texture2D" path="res://assets/textures/fx_plasma_ring.png" id="1"]

[resource]
transparency = 1
blend_mode = 1
cull_mode = 2
shading_mode = 0
albedo_color = Color(1, 1, 1, 1)
albedo_texture = ExtResource("1")
texture_filter = 0
